      "id": "concept-hot-and-cold-proximity-game",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "juego de «frío» y «caliente»",
      "answerEn": "a guessing game in which ‘cold’ means far from the target, ‘warm’ means closer, and ‘hot’ means very close",
      "noteEn": "The handheld unit gives only these proximity clues instead of turn-by-turn directions. Turning the children's guessing game into a navigation system is what makes this an intentionally cheap GPS.",
